CORE no-new-smt
main.c

^\[main.assertion.1\] .* first byte: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] .* first byte of struct: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.3\] .* byte of array element: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.4\] .* overlapping members: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.5\] .* nested union, outer: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.6\] .* nested union: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.7\] .* id copied: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.8\] .* items copied: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.9\] .* code copied: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.10\] .* nondeterministic: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of [0-9]+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Field sensitivity represents a union both by a symbol for the union as a whole
and by symbols for (the fields of) each of its members. For a union that was
declared, but not assigned, these previously had unrelated values, so that the
bytes of the union (as read by memcpy) and its members could differ from each
other.
The incremental SMT back-end does not support arrays within unions.
